    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136">

                <pb facs="0203" n="127" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg127"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.811/231</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to Minister Reinsch
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-11-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 6, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram of September 25. If Foreign Office replied as you anticipated you
                    may support it in that attitude. In any event inform it this Government reserves
                    all American rights.</p>
                <p>Report any further action by Japan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
